    "kind": "agent_answer",
    "from": "repair_agent",
    "text": "The issue `proxy isatty` suggests that when `rich` uses a file proxy (like `FileProxy` in `rich/file_proxy.py`) as its output stream, the `isatty()` method is not correctly implemented or accessible, causing `rich/console.py` to incorrectly determine if the output is a terminal.\n\nIn `rich/file_proxy.py`, `FileProxy` wraps an `IO[str]` file. It should implement `isatty()` to delegate the check to the underlying file object, similar to how `rich/progress.py` handles it for its internal handle.\n\nI will add an `isatty` method to `rich/file_proxy.py`.\n\nFile: `rich/file_proxy.py`\n\n```python\n    def fileno(self) -> int:\n        return self.__file.fileno()\n```\n\nI will add:\n```python\n    def isatty(self) -> bool:\n        return self.__file.isatty()\n```\n\nThis should allow `rich/console.py` to correctly call `isatty()` on the proxy object.\n\nI will use `edit_file` to add this method.<channel|>"
  },
